<a> vatopfn: Given VA you can get its PA using

Remember the output "maps pfn 0x3346ac" is 4k aligned so the real PA is 0x3346ac_000


<b> pte: You can monitor the ptes using the pte command

<c> report_maps: Given PA you can get all the VAs


================
Sample Usage:
================

ffffff00176e2c60::vatopfn
ffffff00176e2c60::vatopfn
        level=0 htable=ffffff03d9f876a0 pte=3346ac163
        level=1 htable=ffffff03d9f87cd0 pte=3822027
        level=2 htable=ffffff03d9f87c88 pte=2e79fe027
        level=3 htable=ffffff03d9f88db0 pte=2e79ff027
Virtual address 0xffffff00176e2c60 maps pfn 0x3346ac



3346ac163::pte
pte=3346ac163: pfn=0x3346ac global write 



3346ac::report_maps
hat=ffffff03d9cdbe78 maps addr=ffffff00176e2000



ffffff00176e2000::dump 
                   \/ 1 2 3  4 5 6 7  8 9 a b  c d e f  v123456789abcdef
ffffff00176e2000:  000490fe 00000000 00000000 00000000  ................



